To identify the most consistent method in terms of hit identification, the Jaccard similarity coefficient of every pair of cell lines in each study was calculated by taking the ratio of intersection of hits over union of hits. For the studies that screened more than two cell lines, the final platform weight was the median of the calculated Jaccard coefficients of all pairs of cell lines.5\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
